pudding I'm making one of my absolute  favorite Italian desserts panna cotta  with that quintessential Italian  flavoring expresser  start by immersing two leaves of  gelatine in cold water and leave to soak  into a small saucepan at Karthus sugar  cream milk sugar and a shot-up good  strong coffee  gently bring to a simmer and remove from  the hob  squeeze out the soap gelatine leaves and  stir into the hot cream until completely  dissolved  pour your cream mixture into a jug and  fill your molds just shorter the rim  rinsing your molds in cold water before  filling will make it easier to get your  panna cotta out once it's set  leaving the fridge for at least two to  three hours or overnight  to make your cinnamon hazelnut brittle  pour castor sugar into a pan and cook  over medium heat until the sugar melts  to a deep golden-brown  scattered toasted hazelnuts into the  caramel dust with ground cinnamon and  leave to set at room temperature  when your panna cotta is firm giving  each mold a quick dip into boiling water  should ensure a perfect stress-free exit  onto the plate  dressed with a shot of crunchy hazelnut  brittle nothing could be so deliciously  elegant
 

